<title>UK: Wachovia Bank prices $250 million 12-year Eurobond.</title>
<headline>Wachovia Bank prices $250 million 12-year Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been priced, lead manager Lehman Brothers International said on Monday.</p>
<p>The deal was launched earlier.</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> BORROWER   WACHOVIA BANK OF NORTH CAROLINA</p>
<p> AMT	  $250 MLN  COUPON     7.0 PCT   MATURITY    17.OCT.08</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.706    PAY DATE    17.OCT.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.40	REOFFER    99.706    SPREAD	+43 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA2	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA+	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.15	SELL CONC  0.25	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND W/I 10-YEAR U.S. TREASURY NOTE</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
